# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# Every commit in this project so far has been made on Windows, and git has
# warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on essentially every file. Without this
# file the working tree's endings leak into the index, so the first person to
# clone on Linux or macOS sees whole files rewritten in the diff and cannot
# tell a real change from an invisible one.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores everything as LF and checks out native, which is
# what the tooling here expects: SUMO's XML, the Python server, the Node test
# scripts and the shell snippets in the README all read the same either way,
# but the diffs stay honest.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated data. Large, machine-written, and not something to review as text
# even when it is technically UTF-8.
*.geojson -diff
sim/net/*.xml -diff
